# This repository is checked out on both Windows and Linux.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set system-wide by Git for Windows on the development
# machine, which would rewrite everything to CRLF on checkout. For Go source
# that is merely untidy. For shell scripts it is fatal, and the failure is
# misleading: a #! line ending in CR makes the kernel report
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", which names the interpreter and
# not the line ending, so the obvious suspect is the wrong one.
#
# So: normalise everything to LF. `eol=lf` is the part that matters — plain
# `* text=auto` still honours core.autocrlf and hands CRLF back on checkout,
# which puts the carriage return straight back into .gitignore and
# .gitattributes themselves.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.go       text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.exe      binary
